<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore non-oil exports down 6.3 pct in August.</title>
<headline>Singapore non-oil exports down 6.3 pct in August.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's non-oil domestic exports fell a nominal 6.3 percent year-on-year in August to Singapore $7.01 billion after rising 6.3 percent in July, the Trade Development Board (TDB) said on Friday.  </p>
<p>A Reuter poll of eight Singapore-based economists had predicted a nominal year-on-year fall of 0.8 percent in August.</p>
<p>In real terms, non-oil exports fell 2.8 percent in August to S$8.94 billion after rising 10.4 percent in July.  </p>
<p>Trade in nominal terms, in bln S$ at current prices</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes given in parentheses)</p>
